34,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found that only two firms can do the big digging. They are worried about the clay. It might be risky.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,The fund only pays for plants and water. It does not pay for paving or buildings. That changes the budget significantly.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The old basin is fine, but the apron outside the hall has been patched three times. Hard surfaces seem to fail faster.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The staff roll is down to seven. We rely on bought-in services for water and turf. It is a thin margin.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"People cross on firm ground, not the soft edges. And the drainage callouts have doubled. The ground is fighting us.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, if the fund doesn't cover paving, that is a big gap. I am worried about the cost of the hard parts.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, exactly. And the upkeep for planted ground is triple the hard surface. It is a double whammy.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shunichi, the drainage issue is serious. If the water is not managed, the plants will die, like on the avenue.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, the avenue trees died because of no aftercare. We have volunteers, but can they handle the water?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the volunteers are good, but the staff is thin. We need a plan that fits the current capacity.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"The phasing notes say we can hoard the south, but not the center. We have to be careful with the layout.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"If we choose a plan with lots of water and plants, the upkeep will be high. We need to be realistic.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. The hard surfaces failed before. Maybe we should focus on what the ground can actually support.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"The volunteer groups are active, but they are not professional. We need a plan that is low maintenance.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The heat readings are high. We need shade, but not at the cost of constant maintenance.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I think we need to look at the candidates now. I am leaning towards something that works with the ground.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,I am concerned about the long-term cost. I will vote for the one that is most sustainable financially.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I will vote for the one that has a track record of lasting. I have seen too many pretty plans fail.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I will vote for the one that the current team can actually manage. We cannot afford to overstretch.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I will vote for the one that fits the way people use the park. It has to be practical.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
